```

Expr root:
```go
type Expr struct {
    Root Node
    matches []*Match  // collected match terms, deduped
    source string
}
func Parse(src string) (*Expr, error)
func (e *Expr) Eval(ctx *Context) bool
func (e *Expr) MatchTerms() []*Match
func (e *Expr) String() string
```

**Lexer**: tokens: IDENT (match, path, entropy, and, or, not — case-insensitive keywords), STRING (double-quoted with Go-ish escapes; also single-quoted?), NUMBER, LPAREN, RPAREN, COMMA, ops: && || ! > >= < <= == !=, AND OR NOT words.

I'll support both word and symbol operators. Strings: double-quoted with backslash escapes (\", \\, \n, \t etc.). Regexes in TOML: users will write dsl in TOML triple-quoted strings so backslashes pass through. In DSL string literal, `"\\d"` → `\d`. Use strconv.Unquote for double-quoted strings — that handles escapes well.

**Parser**: recursive descent with precedence: or < and < not < primary.

```
parseOr:  parseAnd ( (OR|AND?? no) ...
parseOr:  left = parseAnd; for tok in {OR, "||"}: right = parseAnd
parseAnd: left = parseUnary; for tok in {AND, "&&"}: right = parseUnary
parseUnary: if NOT/"!": Not(parseUnary); else parsePrimary
parsePrimary: "(" expr ")" | predicate
predicate: IDENT "match" "(" STRING ["," NUMBER] ")"
         | IDENT "path" "(" STRING ")"
         | IDENT "entropy" CMPOP NUMBER
```

Validation: at least one match term required (else rule produces nothing). Regex compile errors → return error with position. Entropy value must be >= 0.

